    docs(02-brownfield): the click writer interrupts after its drain; only the purge never does
    
    ClickRecorder.close calls shutdownNow after the 5 s drain, which interrupts a running insert;
    that is why a click being written then is reported 'shutdown deadline, outcome unknown'. The
    register's Background work row and DESIGN.md's Asynchronous work row said neither job
    interrupts a JDBC call, which holds only for ClickPurge. Both now state each job's behaviour.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

